{"id": "broken-crown-h823x-e243n-fc2mx", "title": "SIGNETURE - CON X HAFONTIA X REISINGER", "forSale": false, "productDescription": {"text": "Created as part of the Con x Hafontia x Dan Reisinger Estate Collaboration\n\nLimited Edition of 50 Units Till the End of Time\nBlack is Printed on Gildan® Heavy Cotton™ 5.3 oz/yd² | 100% US Cotton\n\nFront and Collar screen-printed design\n\n16 singles\n\nMachine washable, 30 degrees delicate\n\nTo avoid shrinkage, do not machine dry!\n\nMade in USA, Palestine, Israel, Cannan\n\n\nNavy is Printed on Heavyweight 100% Organic Cotton 240GSM Jersey Drop Shoulder Tee \n\nFront screen-printed design\n\nWide crewneck\n\n16 singles\n\nMachine washable, 30 degrees delicate\n\nTo avoid shrinkage, do not machine dry!\n\nMade in USA, Palestine, Israel, China, Turkey, Cannan", "blocks": [{"html": "Created as part of the Con x Hafontia x Dan Reisinger Estate Collaboration", "text": "Created as part of the Con x Hafontia x Dan Reisinger Estate Collaboration", "type": "p"}, {"html": "<strong><u><span>Limited Edition of 50 Units Till the End of Time</span></u></strong><br><strong><u>Black</u></strong> is Printed on Gildan® Heavy Cotton™ 5.3 oz/yd² | 100% US Cotton", "text": "Limited Edition of 50 Units Till the End of Time\nBlack is Printed on Gildan® Heavy Cotton™ 5.3 oz/yd² | 100% US Cotton", "type": "p"}, {"html": "<li><p>Front and Collar screen-printed design</p></li><li><p><span>16 singles</span></p></li><li><p>Machine washable, 30 degrees delicate</p></li><li><p>To avoid shrinkage, do not machine dry!</p></li><li><p>Made in USA, Palestine, Israel, Cannan<br></p></li>", "text": "Front and Collar screen-printed design\n\n16 singles\n\nMachine washable, 30 degrees delicate\n\nTo avoid shrinkage, do not machine dry!\n\nMade in USA, Palestine, Israel, Cannan\n", "type": "ul"}, {"html": "<strong><u>Navy</u></strong> is Printed on Heavyweight 100% Organic Cotton 240GSM <span>Jersey Drop Shoulder Tee </span>", "text": "Navy is Printed on Heavyweight 100% Organic Cotton 240GSM Jersey Drop Shoulder Tee ", "type": "p"}, {"html": "<li><p>Front screen-printed design</p></li><li><p>Wide crewneck</p></li><li><p><span>16 singles</span></p></li><li><p>Machine washable, 30 degrees delicate</p></li><li><p>To avoid shrinkage, do not machine dry!</p></li><li><p>Made in USA, Palestine, Israel, China, Turkey, Cannan</p></li>", "text": "Front screen-printed design\n\nWide crewneck\n\n16 singles\n\nMachine washable, 30 degrees delicate\n\nTo avoid shrinkage, do not machine dry!\n\nMade in USA, Palestine, Israel, China, Turkey, Cannan", "type": "ul"}]}, "projectContent": [{"text": "Con, HaFontia and the Dan Reisinger Estate — a project rooted in the legacy of one of Israel’s most influential graphic designers.\n\nDan Reisinger (1934–2019) was an Israeli artist and graphic designer whose work helped shape the visual language of modern design in Israel and internationally. Reisinger created iconic corporate identities, supergraphics, posters, logos, and cultural symbols that remain central to the visual fabric of the country. His legacy includes, among others, the logos for El Al airlines and Habima National Theatre, as well as a prolific body of graphic work exhibited around the world.  \n\n\nHaFontia, a type foundry and design collective, works to preserve, expand, and reinterpret typographic heritage — including the digital revival and public access to Reisinger’s typographic explorations. This collaboration bridges disciplines and generations, inviting a contemporary engagement with a foundational design legacy.  \n\n\nTogether, Con, HaFontia, and the Dan Reisinger Estate explore the intersections of material culture, visual language, and cultural narrative, celebrating Reisinger’s impact while recontextualizing his work for today’s design discourse.", "blocks": [{"html": "<strong>Con, HaFontia</strong> and the <strong>Dan Reisinger Estate</strong> — a project rooted in the legacy of one of Israel’s most influential graphic designers.", "text": "Con, HaFontia and the Dan Reisinger Estate — a project rooted in the legacy of one of Israel’s most influential graphic designers.", "type": "p"}, {"html": "Dan Reisinger (1934–2019) was an Israeli artist and graphic designer whose work helped shape the visual language of modern design in Israel and internationally. Reisinger created iconic corporate identities, supergraphics, posters, logos, and cultural symbols that remain central to the visual fabric of the country. His legacy includes, among others, the logos for <em>El Al</em> airlines and <em>Habima</em> National Theatre, as well as a prolific body of graphic work exhibited around the world.  <br>", "text": "Dan Reisinger (1934–2019) was an Israeli artist and graphic designer whose work helped shape the visual language of modern design in Israel and internationally. Reisinger created iconic corporate identities, supergraphics, posters, logos, and cultural symbols that remain central to the visual fabric of the country. His legacy includes, among others, the logos for El Al airlines and Habima National Theatre, as well as a prolific body of graphic work exhibited around the world.  \n", "type": "p"}, {"html": "HaFontia, a type foundry and design collective, works to preserve, expand, and reinterpret typographic heritage — including the digital revival and public access to Reisinger’s typographic explorations. This collaboration bridges disciplines and generations, inviting a contemporary engagement with a foundational design legacy.  <br>", "text": "HaFontia, a type foundry and design collective, works to preserve, expand, and reinterpret typographic heritage — including the digital revival and public access to Reisinger’s typographic explorations. This collaboration bridges disciplines and generations, inviting a contemporary engagement with a foundational design legacy.  \n", "type": "p"}, {"html": "Together, <strong>Con, HaFontia, and the Dan Reisinger Estate</strong> explore the intersections of material culture, visual language, and cultural narrative, celebrating Reisinger’s impact while recontextualizing his work for today’s design discourse.", "text": "Together, Con, HaFontia, and the Dan Reisinger Estate explore the intersections of material culture, visual language, and cultural narrative, celebrating Reisinger’s impact while recontextualizing his work for today’s design discourse.", "type": "p"}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 1.jpg", "src": "/media/74c44999a12a-Slide-16_9---1.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 2.jpg", "src": "/media/b6440540ab79-Slide-16_9---2.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 3.jpg", "src": "/media/c17445d680b3-Slide-16_9---3.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 4.jpg", "src": "/media/5daa2ae0feea-Slide-16_9---4.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 5.jpg", "src": "/media/6c4478e12466-Slide-16_9---5.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 6.jpg", "src": "/media/5519b04c3e5b-Slide-16_9---6.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 7.jpg", "src": "/media/7d6f4ccb4304-Slide-16_9---7.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 8.jpg", "src": "/media/790c511b70f2-Slide-16_9---8.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 9.jpg", "src": "/media/9e22220b2804-Slide-16_9---9.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 10.jpg", "src": "/media/98e2e7d9908d-Slide-16_9---10.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "thumb": null}, {"type": "image", "alt": "Slide 16_9 - 11.jpg", "src": "/media/0b743dc0c6ab-Slide-16_9---11.webp", "width": 1920, "height": 108